## Vercel Speed Insights Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the Next.js application following the latest official documentation.

### Changes Made

**1. Installed Package**
   - Added `@vercel/speed-insights` version 2.0.0 to dependencies
   - Updated package-lock.json accordingly

**2. Modified Files**
   - `src/app/layout.tsx`:
     - Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next";`
     - Added `<SpeedInsights />` component in the root layout, placed after the `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag

### Implementation Details

The implementation follows the Next.js App Router pattern (v13.5+) as documented in the official Vercel Speed Insights quickstart guide:
- Used the `@vercel/speed-insights/next` import path for Next.js optimization
- Added the component at the root layout level to ensure it tracks all pages
- Positioned alongside the existing Vercel Analytics component for consistency

### Verification

✅ **Build**: Successfully compiled with no errors (`npm run build`)
✅ **Linter**: No new linting errors introduced in modified files
✅ **Tests**: All 312 tests pass (9 test suites)
✅ **Dependencies**: package-lock.json properly updated

### Next Steps

After deployment to Vercel:
1. Enable Speed Insights in the Vercel dashboard for your project
2. Speed Insights will automatically begin collecting performance metrics
3. Data will be available at `/_vercel/speed-insights/*` routes
4. View metrics in the Vercel dashboard under the Speed Insights tab

### Notes

- The project uses npm as its package manager
- Existing code structure and formatting were preserved
- The SpeedInsights component works alongside the existing PostHog and Vercel Analytics integrations
- No breaking changes or configuration modifications were required
